{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536174-unusual-places-you-have-used-as-a-haven","id":1536174,"title":"Unusual places you have used as a Haven?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-23T17:55:01-07:00","id":1536174,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Unusual places you have used as a Haven?","content":"Myself I had a Gangrel who had a storage unit that he used as a Haven from time to time as he didn't need much in the way of possessions but wanted something else then sleeping in the earth from time to time and he wanted a place for the few precious items he treasured that could be safely hidden. So what places have you used as a Haven that were out of the norm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T22:25:41-07:00","id":1536188,"title":"","content":"So, it was not in VTM, but in a COFD Mortals Oneshot, although, I think it could easily be done in VTM aswell.<br /> <br /> I had a Nosferatu NPC using an old abandoned public indoor bath as a haven. I was inspired by recent liminal horror stuff involving the Poolrooms and &quot;The tale of the deadmans float&quot; if that still rings a bell with someone here.<br /> <br /> With the Lvl 5 Obfuscate Power Oubliette and his Nightmare Discipline it became an earie maze like horror. It was an urban legend and target for dares with the local youth and young adults.<br /> <br /> Thats how my players for that evening stumbled into it. We had a blast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T22:35:29-07:00","id":1536189,"title":"","content":"Their was a tzmisce player who used an zoo elephant as his haven i oncd encountered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T09:01:47-07:00","id":1536208,"title":"","content":"There have been several unusual havens in my games, but usually they are tied to other aspects of the characters rather than being strange for its own sake.<br /> <br /> 1. A sabbat Nosferatu who gained a mastery of Vicissitude ended up turning a Sperm Whale into a living communal haven. The Nosferatu vitae mutated the whale to immense proportions and turned it into a loyal ghoul, while the flesh crafting allowed for add-ons and internal rooms to be created. The coterie would live inside the whale during the day and come ashore every evening. Needless to say, the coterie caused a lot of havoc for shipping and any city on the shoreline.<br /> <br /> 2. A Tremere chantry located in an RV. The small chantry consisted of a few Tremere and a couple ghouls which would move locations during the day and do hacking work during the night. The coterie used the Path of Technomancy and Path of Conjuring to achieve their online goals, which made them very valuable for disrupting markets, governments, or corporations. The RV was upgraded to be more or less bullet proof, heavily warded, and have a few extra gadgets for fun. Thanks to Americas obsession with rest stops and campgrounds along every major road, you don't even need to worry about were-critters all that much.<br /> <br /> 3. Luxury Doomsday Bunker made out of a decommissioned and refurbished missile silo. Decommissioned missile silos cost about $300,000 to purchase, maybe about another $500,000 to renovate to kindred standards/requirements, and you would still have $200,000 left over in the bank if you bought this rather than a standard one-million-dollar home in California. The bunker has 17 or so levels, living quarters for a permanent live in Herd, storage facilities for 5+ years of food, nuclear blast grade security doors, spacious Havens for each vampire, and incredible security. Internet/phone connections mean you can conduct any and all business from your secure haven rather than exposing yourself to the random hazards of kindred society. A mortal or Ghoul security force is on the ground level to deal with anything that might arise. Now imagine such a setup being further enhanced by Tremere warding, Giovanni Necromancy, or Baali demons to name just a few options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T11:23:00-07:00","id":1536266,"title":"","content":"You know Thoth speaking of Doomsday Bunkers. I was watching a new show on HGTV called Zillow Gone Wild and he toured a home that was made in a decommissioned Missile Silo and it was a cool place to live in and I think the owner like bought it for $750,000 and I spent probably the same amount on getting renovated. It would make a cool back up haven for nomadic Ravnos and Gangrels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T11:54:39-07:00","id":1536269,"title":"","content":"I have always seen Ravnos and Country Gangrel as being on the move too much to have anything as elaborate as a doomsday bunker for a backup haven. I think it would be more in keeping with the fluff for them to have a few storage garages at 24 hour storage facilities scattered across the country, probably along their main migration routes or at least near the safest travel corridors.<br /> <br /> Now a City Gangrel on the other hand I could see having some sort of bunker, but it would be in a city rather than being out in the middle of nowhere. An abandoned subway station that has been bricked up or a forgotten 1950s bunker built into the basement of a department store or apartment building that never made it into the city planning records. Though when it comes to Gangrel I think a better term would be a &quot;Den&quot; rather than a proper bunker.<br /> <br /> I had one City Gangrel in a game that was a professional thief, between Obfuscate and Protean they could get almost anywhere and take tons of stuff that was low bulk and high value. While they appreciated the finer things in unlife, like silk sheets, modern plumbing, and the internet, the haven was essentially a room with a big bed in the center and boxes/piles of loot surrounding the bed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T12:47:29-07:00","id":1536523,"title":"","content":"In the last VtM game I ran, two of the PCs slept in the walls of the third's penthouse just to mess with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25998-loneshark","name":"Loneshark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T13:42:04-07:00","id":1536530,"title":"","content":"It was actually Requiem, but regardless.<br /> <br /> One NPC of mine made her haven in a high school... And actually attended.<br /> <br /> She was high enough Humanity to stay awake during the day with some regularity, and kept a student life as a means to keep in touch with mortals and so keep that high Humanity with more ease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T14:01:47-07:00","id":1536643,"title":"","content":"Making a haven in a high school is something I wouldn't consider at all and I thought of using sporting arenas, a ghoul's home and even a prision as possible places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T00:42:15-07:00","id":1536664,"title":"","content":"I think a haven at a college campus would be a better option than a high school. Plenty of night classes to keep you up to date or as plausible deniability. No one questions the idea that you sleep all day and party all night. Plenty of frisky students that would perceive the vampire kiss through their drunken haze as getting lucky. Best of all is that with the high turnover rate of students, unless you stand out too much to the teachers, no one will notice that you don't age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T06:28:06-07:00","id":1536669,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but the question isn't &quot;efficient places you have used as a haven&quot;, and the character specifically wanted to be in highschool for completely personal/emotional reasons as it was a contrast to her previous bad centuries as a low Humanity on the edge of Wassail/Draugr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T12:06:38-07:00","id":1536676,"title":"","content":"Like I said Thoth the topic was unusual havens that have been used instead of the normal places that come to mind. Hence my Gangrel using an storage unit as haven when he wanted to be close to the few items he treasured and some basic luxuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T01:42:45-07:00","id":1536692,"title":"","content":"WoD is a setting that is supposed to be unforgiving and harsh, not total Grim Dark like say Warhammer 40K or Trench Crusade, but not easy to survive regardless of what flavor of splat you are playing. So, ones haven for a Vampire has to have a degree of functionality/efficiency in light of the setting. Otherwise rather than asking for unusual but still functional, you are just asking for quirky and uniquely decorated. <br /> <br /> I brought up the college being a better fit because unless the high school doubles as an adult school at night, the entire campus would be locked down which means a vampire couldn't attend (sunlight) and staying there wouldn't really convey any functional difference from squatting in the air vents of a corporate headquarters or in an unused basement of a department store. Now if there is other backstory that makes it fit better (NPC was light resistant thin-blood?), I am all ears, but just on its own with how it was described it doesn't really make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T11:24:04-07:00","id":1536705,"title":"","content":"I think using a theatre as a haven would be a cool place to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T13:57:28-07:00","id":1536715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536174-unusual-places-you-have-used-as-a-haven?p=1536692#post1536692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WoD is a setting that is supposed to be unforgiving and harsh, not total Grim Dark like say Warhammer 40K or Trench Crusade, but not easy to survive regardless of what flavor of splat you are playing. So, ones haven for a Vampire has to have a degree of functionality/efficiency in light of the setting. Otherwise rather than asking for unusual but still functional, you are just asking for quirky and uniquely decorated.<br /> <br /> I brought up the college being a better fit because unless the high school doubles as an adult school at night, the entire campus would be locked down which means a vampire couldn't attend (sunlight) and staying there wouldn't really convey any functional difference from squatting in the air vents of a corporate headquarters or in an unused basement of a department store. Now if there is other backstory that makes it fit better (NPC was light resistant thin-blood?), I am all ears, but just on its own with how it was described it doesn't really make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because you have a very specific vision of what the harshness of the setting means and entails, and very little patience with people that do things differently than your overly rigid standards that don't let you engage with the proposal of the thread. By the way, standards that fly in the face of the books themselves, as quirky describes most of the settings and NPCs far more than harsh.<br /> <br /> About this character, in the original Requiem version she was sufficiently high Humanity to function during the day as long as she avoided direct sunlight, which is something some rare-but-known health conditions require anyway. In her later Masquerade version she took classes at night, something that several high schools around the world have due to several reasons.<br /> <br /> On both cases the actual haven of this elder was a very safe secret place far below the known corridors of the school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T16:21:47-07:00","id":1536718,"title":"","content":"What comes to mind would be the following places:<br /> <br /> The first isn't even a Haven properly. One player simply had a van that he &quot;bought&quot; from a &quot;former drug dealer&quot; and it had a compartment in the floor that he used to hide &quot;merchandise&quot;, but he expanded this compartment to use as an emergency shelter and made a point of reporting that it was only big enough for one person. In fact, there was a time when he woke up in a towed vehicle parking lot.<br /> <br /> Another once had a Gangrel that had zero dots in resources and therefore slept, in the literature section of the public library. It was supposed to be a joke, but that was never a problem, I don't know if that's very realistic.<br /> <br /> I already had a Toreador who was a college student before the embrace. Her haven was the attic of a disused dormitory, but it still received power and even water, it could be used so much that it didn't attract too much attention. The character was a hacker so she also kept a lot of equipment there, as well as clothes and other amenities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T17:37:54-07:00","id":1536723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536174-unusual-places-you-have-used-as-a-haven?p=1536715#post1536715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because you have a very specific vision of what the harshness of the setting means and entails, and very little patience with people that do things differently than your overly rigid standards that don't let you engage with the proposal of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only person who is being overly harsh, rigid, and showing little patience here is you.<br /> <br /> All I did was comment on a potential setup that would make more sense and you are the one being critical of that. You didn't explain any mechanics until later, and the only requirement for the thread was &quot;unusual&quot; meaning not the standard. I.E. something other than a mansion, castle, or hidden sewer lair. Perhaps it's my age, but I figured the vampire at high school concept got played into the ground back when Buffy the Vampire Slayer was still on TV. To be fair, that could have been before you or the OP were born for all I know.<br /> <br /> As for my views on the harshness of the setting, have you read any of the &quot;Black Dog&quot; imprint White Wolf books? Because that puts the setting closer to survival of the fittest than say My Little Pony and discussions about friendship. Though on second thought, I could totally see a Malkavian using MLP with Dementation to mind break someone so perhaps it does fit. Very much a Death to Smoochy or the childrens entertainer villain from the Netflix &quot;Happy&quot; series kind of behavior.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Forums needs a badge system so that when someone posts, their preferred game type is displayed, like Vampions, grim dark, tactical game play, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536174-unusual-places-you-have-used-as-a-haven?p=1536715#post1536715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, standards that fly in the face of the books themselves, as quirky describes most of the settings and NPCs far more than harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I clearly remember the community at large calling out White Wolf on the concept of the Assamite who made a haven on an american aircraft carrier as being dumb. The sad thing about the Haven book was that the writers were so bad at codifying fluff and mechanics together, which in was turn highlighted by what a good job they did with Oadenols Codex a few years later. Sigh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T19:03:02-07:00","id":1536728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536174-unusual-places-you-have-used-as-a-haven?p=1536692#post1536692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought up the college being a better fit because unless the high school doubles as an adult school at night, the entire campus would be locked down which means a vampire couldn't attend (sunlight) and staying there wouldn't really convey any functional difference from squatting in the air vents of a corporate headquarters or in an unused basement of a department store. Now if there is other backstory that makes it fit better (NPC was light resistant thin-blood?), I am all ears, but just on its own with how it was described it doesn't really make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The high school I went to had plenty of interior hallways and classrooms with no window access to the outside, and even the main cafeteria area wouldn't have had direct sunlight from the adjacent atrium, though reflected light would have been a problem. A vampire could have navigated it safely if they could manage to stay awake through the daytime hours.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T16:00:42-07:00","id":1536764,"title":"","content":"Please let's not get into a flame war as this is meant to be a fun post about unusual havens that you have used in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}